From 6b664b3771a1851bbf6a5ac3608bad379ec11a13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:40:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 210/211] Gatekeeper v1.7.3: fix admin lockout + cold-boot
 non-arm; graceful arming

Field reports: Gatekeeper locked the router (admin could not reach the UI to
disable it) and did not re-arm after a hard reboot. Root causes and fixes:

- Admin lockout: in quarantine mode a held device (incl. a mis-grandfathered
  admin box, or any device asleep at enable time) could reach only DHCP/DNS/
  tcp80 on the router, fencing the admin off from the UI that disables the
  feature. Fix: REAPER_GKI always RETURNs the admin port (HTTPS via the httpd
  do_ssl carve-out, or the plain-HTTP admin port on an HTTP-only router with
  the captive redirect suppressed); the baseline snapshot now grandfathers
  ARP + DHCP leases + custom_clientlist so idle/known devices are not held.

- Cold-boot non-arm: apply.sh baked lan_ifname at generation time; on a cold
  boot start_gk ran before the bridge existed, so rules never hooked and the
  firewall/self-heal paths only re-ran the stale file. Fix: apply.sh resolves
  LANIF/LANIP/admin-port at run time and defers cleanly (exit 1) until the
  bridge is up; start_gk logs the deferral; gkd self-heal re-runs it and arms.

- Graceful failure / visibility: gkd maintains /tmp/gk/chains.ok and the status
  CGI exposes "armed"; the page shows an amber "Arming" state that escalates to
  a red "Not enforcing - check System Log" fault if it persists. stop_gk clears
  the stamp on disable.

Addresses a 3-agent adversarial review (admin lockout, HTTP-only hatch, stale
stamp, respawn re-log, broadcast MAC, 443 fallback, DNAT LANIP guard, UI
escalation). Built clean for RT-BE96U (MCP variant); on-metal exercise owed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
